      "description": "India and the US have already agreed that Indian goods in the American market will receive preferential market access compared to competitor nations, Commerce and Industry Minister Piyush Goyal said on Sunday.\nIndia and the US finalised the framework for the first phase of the bilateral trade agreement in February.\nThe deal was to be signed earlier, but changes in the US tariff landscape have led to further negotiations on the agreement.\n\"This was already agreed between the leaders - President (Donald) Trump and Prime Minister Narendra Modi when they announced that we have both come to a broad framework agreement a few months ago and it has been acknowledged that India will get preferential trade access in the US with lower duties than our competitor countries,\" Goyal told reporters here.\nHe is here on a two-day visit to discuss ways to boost trade and investment between India and Egypt.\nThe minister was replying to a question about the US assurance that Indian goods will get ...",
